;; The appliance on a machine QEMU actually models.
;;
;; The CM5 and Pi images cannot be booted in QEMU: there is no bcm2712 machine,
;; and QEMU's Raspberry Pi support stops at the Pi 4. That is not a limitation
;; worth working around, because an image is a board plus a userspace, and only
;; the board half is missing. Compose the same features onto target:qemu-aarch64-virt
;; and the same device answers on the same ports, on a machine that exists.
;;
;; Which is the argument for the language in its cheapest form: the appliance
;; is four features, the board is one fragment, and swapping the board is what
;; this file does.
;;
;; What it is for. Continuous integration, because a protocol regression should
;; be caught by a machine rather than by flashing a card. A demonstration
;; anybody can run without hardware. And an evaluation image: someone deciding
;; whether this device is worth buying can boot it in QEMU first, which is a
;; better answer than a screenshot.
;;
;;   qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 512 -nographic \
;;     -kernel build/images/Image -drive file=build/images/rootfs.ext4,if=none,id=hd \
;;     -device virtio-blk-device,drive=hd -append "root=/dev/vda console=ttyAMA0" \
;;     -netdev user,id=n,hostfwd=tcp::5020-:502,hostfwd=tcp::4840-:4840,hostfwd=tcp::8080-:8080 \
;;     -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n
;;
;; Then mbpoll, uaread and curl against localhost, on 5020, 4840 and 8080.
;;
;; No feature:dev-ssh here. The console is the console, and a key baked into an
;; image anyone can download is worse than no key at all.
;;
;; profile:standard rather than profile:minimal, and the checker is why. minimal
;; states BR2_STATIC_LIBS, kmod has depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS, and
;; feature:fieldbus-test needs kmod because BusyBox modprobe cannot read the
;; xz-compressed modules the Pi kernels build. Composing the appliance onto the
;; smaller profile is refused with all three lines named - the same shape as the
;; libcamera conflict this project opens with, met while writing this file.

(image qemu-arm-appliance
  (compose
    target:qemu-aarch64-virt
    profile:standard
    feature:networking
    feature:modbus
    feature:fieldbus-test)

  ;; As qemu-arm-dev explains at length: this board directory's patch set
  ;; serves every QEMU target, MIPS included, and applying it here breaks the
  ;; build before anything is compiled.
  (opaque
    (value buildroot:BR2_ROOTFS_POST_IMAGE_SCRIPT "board/qemu/post-image.sh")
    (value buildroot:BR2_ROOTFS_POST_SCRIPT_ARGS  "$(BR2_DEFCONFIG)"))

  (unmanaged
    buildroot:BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_*
    buildroot:BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_CONFIG_*)

  ;; CI boots this one. It is the only appliance a machine can run without
  (ci boot)

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
